            "review_title": "Review at Am Thuc Xeo Vo Van Kiet",
            "review_text": "Stanley H\nHong Kong, China11223 contributions\n0\nPack your own milk\nDec 2024 • Family\nThat day, the team came to a seemingly cheerful restaurant called Xèo. According to literal translation, it is said that this is the specialty of Hong Kong food. And this is also a meal introduced by the tour group, the experience of rice paper.\n\nTo the second floor, it was a good huge dining building. It can also be seen that this is a place where the camp can be held. And this day, it is the noon time, sitting in the restaurant, greeting, seems to be all visitors. Believe me, this restaurant's bagel roll experience is probably a designated activity for every traveler who comes with you to Hong Kong.\n\nWhen food does not arrive, each person has a huge glass of cool drinks. A cup of aromatic tea. Frozen and sweet. Plus this drink has indeed an aromatic taste. It feels better if you enjoy this drink on hot days.\n\nBecause it is a trip meal, the vegetarian care of the wife is necessary in advance. And this restaurant serves sausage. In addition, there is also a vegetarian powder, cream tomatoes. The wife said, again a rich meal of weight gain.\n\nAnd our meal begins with this fragranced chain. Whether in Vietnam or in Hong Kong, I have eaten a couple of times like this, I am surprised how the maker can bring this meat bag to reality. And when we put this string in the mouth, the taste is fragile, and there is also a intense fragrance.\n\nAs the shopkeeper was busy cooking, suddenly a plate of green dishes came. And in Southeast Asia, cooking is the most common thing. Cool cuisine, with garlic aroma, will not eat badly.\n\nThen came something like a baking cake. At this time, the guide to speak. Let everyone not rush to put this thing in the mouth, because, this is one of the saucers we want to experience, to learn, their own rice wrap their own bag.\n\nThen the shopkeeper put a roll of rice paper on the counter. The guide spoke again, telling us not to rush. A shopkeeper will come to teach everyone how to make a Vietnamese paper roll.\n\nIn a moment, the beauty shopkeeper came. She taught everyone to make authentic Vietnamese spring rolls. And the tour guide brother stood next to him, responsible for translating to everyone.\n\nThis Vietnamese paper spring roll, first pack a layer of rice, add the dish, then the fragile baking cake with the meat, and then into the carrots and wheat, is a wonderful Vietnamese paper spring roll. Because of the convenience of sitting close, our family can enjoy the spring roll of paper in the hands of beauty shopkeepers.\n\nAfterwards, there are two flavors of rice. This is a specialty of central Vietnamese pie, called Fauvin. One, add something similar to the cowboard, soak the rice in the sauce oil. Another, soak in a sauce with beans. The taste is outstanding, and the rice is soft and fragrant. It is a good wonderful food.\n\nI have eaten my own pack of cold Vietnamese spring roll. Afterwards, at the end of the shop came a hot meal of Vietnamese cooking roll. Broken spring roll, is the meat and oatmeal pie, eaten to taste delicious. Of course, the taste is also abundant.\n\nFinally, it is Vietnamese powder that everyone likes. This time we ate chicken powder. Chicken soup base, directly make the meat and soup taste full. And the river powder is strong, and the juice absorption ability is very strong. Definitely a delicious bowl of Phở.\n\nAlthough this seems to be a restaurant dedicated to greeting visitors, the scene is cheerful, the food is of high quality and it is already a joy. Maybe the shopkeepers aren't enough to make the service a little mismatched, but everyone is happy to eat, it's good. After we ate enough, we officially visited Hong Kong.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Chinese\nShow original\nWritten April 10, 2025",
